course: dictionary
lesson: 11093
title: Whatever and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word whatever can do different jobs in a sentence. Sometimes it means anything or everything that: «Take whatever you need» means take all the things you need, whichever they are.
explain: Sometimes it means no matter what: «Whatever happens, stay calm.» The sentence says to stay calm even if something bad or surprising happens. Read the words around whatever to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Whatever can also sound rude. Said alone as «Whatever!», it means "I don't care". «Short answers like "whatever" can be about how someone feels inside, not about you.» A short reply may show that someone is tired or upset, but it is still kinder to say what you really think.
fact: Whatever can be a pronoun, a determiner, an adverb or an informal interjection.
fact: «Whatever» can mean anything or everything that, as in «Take whatever you need».
fact: «Whatever» can mean no matter what, as in «Whatever happens, stay calm».
fact: At the end of a list, whatever means or something like that.
fact: Said alone, «Whatever!» means I don't care, and it often sounds rude. «Whatever it takes» means doing everything that is needed.
exercise: «Some people stay grumpy whatever you do; then it is fine to play somewhere else.» In this sentence, whatever means | I don't care, said rudely | *no matter what | only just | or something like that
exercise: Mia says, "We could go to the park, the shops, or whatever." What does whatever mean at the end of the list? | I don't care | Anything that is broken | No matter what | *Or something like that
exercise: Ben says "Whatever!" to his friend and walks off. What does this usually suggest? | *I don't care, and it can sound rude | Please repeat that more slowly | I am very happy about your idea | Let us all go home now
test: «Power is split into three parts so that no one person can do whatever they like.» Here whatever means | *anything or everything that they choose | or something like that | I don't care | no matter what happens
test: In «Take whatever you need», what word class is whatever? | Interjection | Adverb | Verb | *Pronoun
exam: «Whatever else two children argue about, who crossed into the other's space is a fact you can check.» Here whatever means | *no matter what else | I don't care, said rudely | or something like that | anything at the end of a list
